{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git status --short --branch; git log -4 --oneline; cat test/yin/repl/dht_args_test.cljc'","aggregated_output":"## store-swap-p1...origin/master [ahead 1, behind 2]\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795360785000-architect-store-swap-design.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795361680000-engineer-store-swap-p1.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795361680000-engineer-store-swap-p1.gpt-6.2-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795361680000-engineer-store-swap-p1.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795364000000-reviewer-store-swap-p1-gate.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795364000000-reviewer-store-swap-p1-gate.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795364000000-reviewer-store-swap-p1-gate.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795364600000-engineer-store-swap-p2.gpt-6.2-sol.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795364600000-engineer-store-swap-p2.gpt-6.2-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795364600000-engineer-store-swap-p2.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795370000000-reviewer-store-swap-p2-gate.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795370000000-reviewer-store-swap-p2-gate.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795370000000-reviewer-store-swap-p2-gate.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795372400000-engineer-store-swap-p4-docs.gemini-4-argon-high.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795372400000-engineer-store-swap-p4-docs.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795372400000-engineer-store-swap-p4-docs.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795373400000-reviewer-store-swap-p4-gate.glm-5.3.findings.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795373400000-reviewer-store-swap-p4-gate.glm-5.3.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795373400000-reviewer-store-swap-p4-gate.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795374300000-architect-store-swap-signoff.gemini-4-argon-high.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795374300000-architect-store-swap-signoff.prompt.md\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795380000000-engineer-store-swap-dart-args-fix.gpt-6.2-sol.stdout.log\n?? collab/yin-repl/1795380000000-engineer-store-swap-dart-args-fix.prompt.md\n13a94312 feat(yin.repl): in-session dao.jing store switching — (use-store ...) with quiesce gate and strict open-first swap\nea8e8e15 docs(collab): brief for the receiving orchestrator — in-session dao.jing store switching for yin.repl (feature; Architect round first; options named, Gambit C4 boundary binding)\nacdbba94 merge: reconcile the arc-log branch with master's newest landings\nda7f4d44 docs(orchestrator-log): post-P2-prime triage — the dao.host gate red triaged, fixed via the jolt seat, countersigned and landed\n(ns yin.repl.dht-args-test\n  \"Subcommand expansion is host-free, including flags before the command.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n            [yin.repl.main :as main]\n            [yin.shell.cli :as cli]\n            [yin.shell.main :as shell]))\n\n\n(def principal (apply str (repeat 64 \"a\")))\n(def token (str \"yin:127.0.0.1:4001/\" principal))\n\n\n(deftest join-after-global-flags-keeps-the-explicit-store\n  (doseq [argv [[\"--index-store\" \"dht:reader\" \"--headless\" \"dht\" \"join\" token]\n                [\"dht\" \"join\" \"--index-store\" \"dht:reader\" \"--headless\" token]\n                [\"dht\" \"join\" token \"--index-store\" \"dht:reader\" \"--headless\"]]]\n    (let [[args extra] (cli/expand-args argv)\n          opts (shell/parse-args args)\n          spec (:index-store-spec opts)]\n      (is (= \"reader\" (:dir spec)))\n      (is (:headless? opts))\n      (is (= [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 4001}] (:peers spec)))\n      (is (= [principal] (:principals opts)))\n      (is (= [{:principal principal :host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 4001}]\n             (:follow spec)))\n      (is (= #{\"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-key\"} (:unset extra))))))\n\n\n(deftest init-and-serve-after-global-flags-expand-like-command-first\n  (doseq [verb [\"init\" \"serve\"]]\n    (let [tail [\"--dir\" \"node\" \"--key\" \"node.key\" \"--listen\" \"4002\"\n                \"--peer\" \"127.0.0.1:4001\"]\n          prefixed (cli/expand-args (into [\"--vm\" \"cesk\" \"dht\" verb] tail))\n          ordinary (cli/expand-args (into [\"dht\" verb] (into tail [\"--vm\" \"cesk\"])))]\n      (is (= ordinary prefixed)))))\n\n\n(deftest a-global-flag-value-is-never-a-subcommand\n  (doseq [args [[\"--index-store\" \"dht\"] [\"--index-store\" \"keygen\"]\n                [\"--name\" \"dht\" \"--index-store\" \"mem\"]]]\n    (is (= (main/plain-args args) (cli/expand-args args)))))\n\n\n(deftest startup-expands-the-supplied-reader-command-before-parsing\n  (let [seen (atom nil)\n        composition (assoc shell/composition\n                           :open (fn [spec _]\n                                   (reset! seen spec)\n                                   {:index-store nil}))\n        started (main/startup\n                  [\"--reset\" \"--index-store\" \"dht:reader\" \"dht\" \"join\" token]\n                  {:persist? false :composition composition})]\n    (is (nil? (:refusal started)))\n    (is (= [{:host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 4001}] (:peers @seen)))\n    (is (= [{:principal principal :host \"127.0.0.1\" :port 4001}]\n           (:follow @seen)))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '308,334p;373,470p' src/cljc/yin/shell/cli.cljc; sed -n '647,759p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '251,316p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; rg -n ':load-key \\\\(|:publisher-key-file|:index-store nil' test/yin/repl/{main,dht_args,dht}_test.cljc | head -45; rg -n 'deftest|:no-state' test/yin/repl/dht_args_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '308,334p;373,470p' src/cljc/yin/shell/cli.cljc; sed -n '647,759p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; sed -n '251,316p' src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc; rg -n ':load-key \\\\(|:publisher-key-file|:index-store nil' test/yin/repl/{main,dht_args,dht}_test.cljc | head -45; rg -n 'deftest|:no-state' test/yin/repl/dht_args_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"\n(defn home-dir*\n  \"The user's home directory, or nil where the host has none (ClojureDart).\"\n  []\n  #?(:cljd nil\n     :clj (System/getProperty \"user.home\")\n     :cljs (some-> js/process .-env .-HOME)))\n\n\n(defn home-dir\n  []\n  (or (home-dir*)\n      (throw (ex-info (str \"no home directory on this host: give --dir and \"\n                           \"--key explicitly\")\n                      {}))))\n\n\n(defn state-path\n  \"`~/.yin/<name><suffix>`.\"\n  [name suffix]\n  (str (home-dir) \"/.yin/\" name suffix))\n\n\n(defn- peer-text\n  \"A peer as the DHT takes it: `localhost` is the loopback IP literal.\"\n  [text]\n  (str/replace-first (str text) #\"^localhost:\" \"127.0.0.1:\"))\n\n(defn- global-flag-kind\n  [arg]\n  (or (get (:kinds flag-table) arg)\n      (when (contains? (:one-shot-flags flag-table) arg) :value)\n      (get {\"--name\" :value \"--dir\" :value\n            \"--reset\" :switch \"--no-state\" :switch} arg)))\n\n\n(defn- dht-args\n  \"The legacy flags of `dht init|serve|join`.  `init` publishes (its key is\n   made on first use); `serve` stores for others; `join <token>` reads,\n   declaring and following the token's principal at its address.\n   Every node needs a `--peer` to open a socket (the two-node start in\n   yin.repl.md); `--listen [ip:]port` is the node's own address.  Returns\n   `[args {:new-key path}]`.\"\n  [[verb & args]]\n  (when-not (#{\"init\" \"serve\" \"join\"} verb)\n    (throw (ex-info \"usage: yin-repl dht init|serve|join [token] [options]\"\n                    {})))\n  (loop [args (seq args)\n         o {:name \"node\" :peers [] :rest []}]\n    (if-let [arg (first args)]\n      (let [v (second args)]\n        (case arg\n          \"--name\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :name v))\n          \"--dir\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :dir v))\n          \"--key\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :key v))\n          \"--peer\" (recur (nnext args) (update o :peers conj (peer-text v)))\n          \"--listen\" (recur (nnext args) (assoc o :listen v))\n          (let [kind (global-flag-kind arg)]\n            (cond\n              (and kind (not= :switch kind))\n              (recur (nnext args) (update o :rest into [arg v]))\n\n              (and (= \"join\" verb) (not (:token o))\n                   (not (str/starts-with? arg \"-\")))\n              (recur (next args) (assoc o :token arg))\n\n              :else (recur (next args) (update o :rest conj arg))))))\n      (let [{:keys [name dir key peers listen token rest]} o\n            [tpeer principal] (when (= \"join\" verb)\n                                (parse-token token))\n            tpeer (some-> tpeer peer-text)\n            peers (cond-> peers tpeer (conj tpeer))\n            [_ lhost lport] (when listen\n                              (re-matches #\"(?:(.+):)?(\\d+)\" listen))\n            key (or key (when (= \"init\" verb) (state-path name \".key\")))]\n        [(cond-> [\"--index-store\" (str \"dht:\" (or dir (state-path name \"\")))]\n           (= \"init\" verb) (conj \"--dht-publish\")\n           key (into [\"--dht-key\" key])\n           lhost (into [\"--dht-bind\" lhost])\n           lport (into [\"--dht-port\" lport])\n           ;; join follows the principal's head at the token's address and\n           ;; passes no manifest: its first manifest is the first head it\n           ;; installs (yin.vm.linker.dht.head.md 5.8)\n           principal (into [\"--dht-principal\" principal\n                            \"--dht-follow\" (str principal \"@\" tpeer)])\n           true (into (mapcat #(vector \"--dht-peer\" %)) peers)\n           true (into rest))\n         {:new-key (when (= \"init\" verb) key)\n          :name name\n          :dir (or dir (state-path name \"\"))\n          ;; only `init` publishes and signs by default: a saved --dht-publish\n          ;; or --dht-key must not survive `serve` or `join` (explicit flags\n          ;; named on that command line still stand)\n          :unset (when-not (= \"init\" verb) #{\"--dht-publish\" \"--dht-key\"})}]))))\n\n\n(defn expand-args\n  \"Turn the subcommand surface into the flags `parse-args` reads:\n   `keygen [--name n | file]` and `dht init|serve|join`.  Anything else\n   passes to the engine's own plain form (`--name n` and `--dir d`, which\n   name the node directory its state file lives in). DHT subcommands may\n   follow global flags; their values are skipped as values, never treated\n   as commands. Explicit flags override the subcommand's defaults. Answers\n   `[args extra]`, `extra` carrying what the arguments say beyond flags:\n   `:new-key` (a key file `init` makes), `:name` and `:dir` (the node\n   directory), and `:unset` (saved flags the subcommand clears).\"\n  [args]\n  (loop [more (seq args) prefix []]\n    (let [arg (first more)\n          kind (global-flag-kind arg)]\n      (cond\n        (= \"dht\" arg)\n        (dht-args (cons (second more) (concat prefix (nnext more))))\n\n        (and (empty? prefix) (= \"keygen\" arg))\n        [(keygen-args (rest more)) nil]\n\n        kind\n        (let [n (if (= :switch kind) 1 2)]\n          (recur (drop n more) (into prefix (take n more))))\n\n        :else (repl.main/plain-args args)))))\n\n\n(defn parse-flag\n        [(str \"state: WARNING: could not save \" path \": \"\n              (or (ex-message e) (str e)))]))))\n\n\n(defn startup\n  \"Parse the arguments and compose the whole shell (the store the parsed\n   `:index-store-spec` names included), or answer the refusal text.  This\n   is the one gate every host's `-main` passes through before it prints a\n   banner or starts a loop, so an invalid `--index-store`, an unsupported\n   host for it, or a directory that cannot be opened refuses startup with\n   its reason rather than composing a shell around a fallback store.\n\n   Only a designed refusal is answered: an error carrying no ex-info\n   keeps its stack trace, because it is a defect, not an operator error.\n\n   `:composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage composition\n   (`parse-args`' and `boot`'s argument of the same name): its flags, its\n   subcommands, its key file, its help and banner text, its store and its\n   transport lifecycle.  Every one of those reaches this gate through that\n   value and none of them is named here, so a host that carries no\n   composition has the engine's own surface and nothing more.  A\n   composition's `:keygen-flag` names the one argument that composes\n   nothing at all: it writes a key file through `:keygen!` and answers\n   `{:lines [...] :exit 0}` for the host to print and exit with, and no\n   state file is read or written for such a run.  A key file named on the\n   command line is loaded by `:load-key` here, and reaches `boot` as\n   `:publisher-key`.\n\n   `:adapter` is the host WebSocket adapter the shell, the composition's\n   own endpoints and the served endpoint compose over (else\n   `host/websocket`).  `:flag-table` is the `state/flag-table` the saved\n   state is read, split, described and written by: an explicit table when\n   the caller hands one in, else the composition's, else the engine's own.\"\n  ([args] (startup args nil))\n  ([args {:keys [persist? home adapter flag-table composition]}]\n   (try\n     (if (some #{\"--help\" \"-h\"} args)\n       {:lines (or (:help-lines composition) help-lines) :exit 0}\n       (let [reset? (boolean (some #{\"--reset\"} args))\n             no-state? (boolean (some #{\"--no-state\"} args))\n             table (or flag-table (composition-flag-table composition))\n             keygen-flag (:keygen-flag composition)\n             [args {:keys [new-key unset] node-name :name dir :dir}]\n             (expand-args (remove #{\"--reset\" \"--no-state\"} args) composition)\n             node-dir (when (and persist? (not no-state?)\n                                 (not (and keygen-flag\n                                           (some #{keygen-flag} args))))\n                        (or dir\n                            (some-> (or home (home-dir*))\n                                    (str \"/.yin/\" node-name))))\n             saved (when (and node-dir (not reset?))\n                     (state/load-flags node-dir table))\n             {:keys [flags rest]} (state/split-args args table)\n             resolved (state/resolve-flags saved flags unset)\n             args (into (state/flags->args resolved table) rest)\n             made (when (and new-key (:ensure-key! composition))\n                    ((:ensure-key! composition) new-key))\n             opts (cond-> (try (parse-args args composition)\n                               (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                                         :clj Throwable\n                                         :cljs :default)\n                                      e\n                                 (throw (if (and saved (ex-data e))\n                                          (ex-info (str (ex-message e)\n                                                        \" (with the saved state in \"\n                                                        (state/path node-dir)\n                                                        \"; --reset forgets it)\")\n                                                   (ex-data e))\n                                          e))))\n                    made (assoc :startup-lines made)\n                    adapter (assoc :adapter adapter))]\n         (if-some [path (:keygen opts)]\n           ((:keygen! composition) path)\n           (let [key (when-some [path (:publisher-key-file opts)]\n                       ((:load-key composition) path))\n                 opts (cond-> opts key (assoc :publisher-key key))\n                 state' (boot (assoc opts\n                                     :ws-host (or (:adapter opts)\n                                                  (host/websocket)))\n                              composition)\n                 server (boot-server opts)\n                 lines (into (composition-startup-lines state')\n                             (when node-dir\n                               (save-state! node-dir saved resolved reset?\n                                            table)))]\n             {:opts (cond-> opts\n                      (seq lines) (update :startup-lines\n                                          #(into (vec %) lines)))\n              :state state'\n              :server server}))))\n     (catch #?(:cljd Object\n               :clj Throwable\n               :cljs :default)\n            e\n       (if (ex-data e)\n         {:refusal (or (ex-message e) (str e))}\n         (throw e))))))\n\n\n(defn- refuse!\n  \"Print why the composition refused to start and end the process with a\n   failing status, so a refused startup never looks like a working shell.\"\n  [refusal]\n  (println refusal)\n  #?(:cljd (io/exit 1)\n     :jolt (do (flush) (System/exit 1))\n     :clj (.halt (Runtime/getRuntime) 1)\n     :cljs (.exit js/process 1)))\n\n\n(defn- custody-of\n  [state]\n  (get-in state [:repl :custody]))\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ nil))))\n\n\n(declare swap-store)\n\n\n(defn boot\n  \"Create the composition: one shell, one input medium, one cursor held only by\n   the step owner, and the host WebSocket adapter `(connect ...)` attaches\n   through.  A custody composition (:custody, yin.vm.ucf.compose) rides the\n   shell as data; the step owner below is the only thing that steps it.\n\n   `composition` is the plain-data contribution of a storage composition\n   past the engine's own two stores.  When it names the parsed\n   `:index-store-spec` as one of its own (`:composition-spec?`), `:open`\n   opens it and answers the two values of the ownership split: `:index-store`,\n   the generic `dao.jing` handle the engine is constructed with, and\n   `:session`, the transport state the composition keeps and steps beside\n   the engine — never inside it.  What the engine additionally needs to\n   drive that store arrives as `:engine-inputs` of the same answer (a\n   prepared `:link-source`, the composition's `:host-modules`), so a\n   `(reset)` or a `(vm ...)` rebuild reconstructs a session that still\n   resolves signed names and still serves the composition's modules.\n\n   The engine value lands at `:repl`, where the driver and the endpoint\n   read it, and the composition's transport state at `:session`; there is\n   no third place a node could hide.  A construction that fails after the\n   store was opened releases what it acquired (`release-store!`) and\n   answers its own refusal.\n\n   `:admission` is the session's admission policy, by default `{}`: the\n   publisher key's own principal only.  It is apart from `:principals`: a\n   declared publisher is not a trusted one.\"\n  ([opts] (boot opts nil))\n  ([opts composition]\n   (let [spec (:index-store-spec opts)\n         open (:open composition)\n         composition-spec? (:composition-spec? composition)\n         comp-store (when (and open composition-spec?\n                               (composition-spec? spec))\n                      (open spec opts))\n         repl-inputs (cond-> (if comp-store\n                               (merge {:index-store (:index-store comp-store)\n                                       :recovery (:recovery comp-store)\n                                       :publication-policy\n                                       (:publication-policy comp-store)}\n                                      (:engine-inputs comp-store))\n                               {:index-store-spec spec})\n                       true (assoc :publisher-key (:publisher-key opts)\n                                   :principals (:principals opts)\n                                   :admission (:admission opts {})\n                                   :custody (:custody opts))\n                       (:vm-type opts) (assoc :vm-type (:vm-type opts)))\n         state (try\n                 (driver/create-state\n                   {:host (or (:adapter opts) (host/websocket))\n                    :repl (repl.frontends/create-state repl-inputs)})\n                 (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                   (when comp-store (release-store! composition comp-store))\n                   (throw e)))]\n     (cond-> (assoc state :composition composition :swap-store swap-store)\n       (:session comp-store) (assoc :session (:session comp-store))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition session\ntest/yin/repl/dht_args_test.cljc:49:                                   {:index-store nil}))\n3:  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is]]\n13:(deftest join-after-global-flags-keeps-the-explicit-store\n29:(deftest init-and-serve-after-global-flags-expand-like-command-first\n38:(deftest a-global-flag-value-is-never-a-subcommand\n44:(deftest startup-expands-the-supplied-reader-command-before-parsing\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
